# upstream/91-buffer-type-iterative: getBufferType computes buffer types
# from an explicit stack, so its native depth does not grow with the length
# of a chain of values whose buffer types depend on each other, and the
# bufferization of arrays keeps a small stack. An scf.for carrying an
# allocated tensor through 5,000 pairs of tensor.cast, on a thread whose
# stack is 256 KiB: its result, its iter_arg and the value it yields each
# have the allocation's buffer type, memref<4xf32>, as the recursion gave
# them (buffer-type.cpp). The chain is flat, so it is the computation alone
# that a frame per value would overflow.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "buffer type: a loop carrying a tensor through 10,000 casts on a 256 KiB stack, its result, iter_arg and yielded value each the allocation's memref<4xf32>" \
  "$here/buffer-type.cpp" 5000
